.TH SHIFTS-API-PROBE 1 "2026-11-06" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler v1.1.0" "Mu2e Shift Scheduler"
.SH NAME
shifts_api_probe.py \- query the Mu2e Shift Scheduler token API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/shifts_api_probe.py
[\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-token\fR \fITOKEN\fR]
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIon-duty\fR|\fIclassifications\fR|\fIschedules\fR|\fIhealth\fR]
[\fB\-\-at\fR \fIISO\fR]
[\fB\-\-classification\fR \fISLUGS\fR]
[\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISEC\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
[\fB\-\-insecure\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Diagnostic client for the bearer-token JSON API served under
.IR /api/v1 .
It first calls
.I /api/v1/health
(no token), then the requested endpoint with
.BR "Authorization: Bearer" .
Use it to confirm a token minted on the Admin > API Tokens page works
against a deployment, or to see exactly what the bulletin board will receive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-url " URL"
Scheduler base URL. Default: \fBSHIFTS_API_URL\fR, else
.IR http://127.0.0.1:8001 .
.TP
.BI \-\-token " TOKEN"
Bearer token. Default: \fBSHIFTS_API_TOKEN\fR from the environment or
.IR .env .
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " NAME"
Which endpoint to call. Default
.BR on-duty .
.TP
.BI \-\-at " ISO"
Datetime for \fBon-duty\fR (ISO-8601, naive = America/Chicago). Default: now.
.TP
.BI \-\-classification " SLUGS"
Comma-separated classification slugs to keep, e.g.
.IR run-coordinators,oncall-daq-experts .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the raw JSON body instead of the formatted table.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Skip TLS certificate verification (local test instances only).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 transport or server error; 2 usage error; 3 token rejected (401).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
    scripts/shifts_api_probe.py --base-url https://mu2e-shifts.fnal.gov --token mu2e_abc...
    SHIFTS_API_TOKEN=mu2e_abc... scripts/shifts_api_probe.py --at 2026-11-06T22:00 --json
    scripts/shifts_api_probe.py --endpoint classifications
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2e-shift-scheduler (1),
.I docs/API.md
